use Libraries.Web.Page.QuorumPage

/*
    Spatial Sounds.
    Converted from the old Lesson page by plan 13's generator: the same
    words, now without Tailwind.
*/
class SpatialSounds is QuorumPage

    on create
        SetLocation("lessons/Scenes/spatial.html")
        // The name lists and links use, and the series and track it belongs
        // to: its section and picture.
        SetShortTitle("Spatial Sounds")
        SetSectionName("Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ)")
        // For search engines and link previews, and what lists of pages say.
        SetDescription("Learn to use spatial sound with the Quorum programming language.")
        SetSummary(" spatial sound in a running game.")
    end

    action Setup
        SetWebPageTitle("Spatial Sounds - Quorum Programming Language")
        Title("Spatial Sounds")
        Paragraph("Use arrays and loops to prepare ourselves for spatial sound")
        LearningObjectives()
        RefactorExistingCodeToUseArrays10Minutes()
        Repeat15Minutes()
        FindTheClosestItemToThePlayer10Minutes()
        InvestigateSpatializedSound10Minutes()
    end

    private action LearningObjectives
        Section("Learning Objectives")
        Paragraph("In this lesson, we are going to use our new knowledge of arrays to clean up our code, eventually letting us work toward adding spatial sound. We often need to understand concepts like arrays, however, to begin to understand how sound works in the computer. Thus in this tutorial, we are first going to focus on converting our code to use arrays.")
        Paragraph("You will:")
        BulletList()
        ListItem("Learn about refactoring, the process of changing around existing code")
        ListItem("Learn about looping using repeat")
        ListItem("Learn about spatial sound")
    end

    private action RefactorExistingCodeToUseArrays10Minutes
        Section("Refactor Existing Code to Use Arrays (10 Minutes)")
        Paragraph("The items for our quest are stored so far in individual variables. We want to change this to clean up our code. As a first step, we are going to declare an Array, like so:")
        Paragraph("For 2D use:")
        CodeExample("Array<Item2D> goodItems")
        Paragraph("For 3D use:")
        CodeExample("Array<Item3D> goodItems")
        Paragraph("These declarations tells us that we want an array and the type is either Item2D or Item3D, which is what the Scene Editor stores. By making this declaration, we can then fill the array and manipulate these items.")
    end

    private action Repeat15Minutes
        Section("Repeat (15 minutes)")
        Paragraph("One big advantage of data structures like arrays is that we can loop over them, which means we can ask the computer to do the same code on each one of them. In essence, we tell our program we want to Hide a bunch of items, instead of calling Hide on each one individually. This reduces code duplication and requires we learn about "):Link("repeat", "/tutorials/language/repeat.html"):Text(".")
    end

    private action FindTheClosestItemToThePlayer10Minutes
        Section("Find the Closest Item to the Player (10 minutes)")
        Paragraph("In computer science, we often create what are called algorithms, which are essentially steps for solving problems. Using our distance equation we used in a previous lesson, or a new one, use a loop to figure out which of the items we are looking for is closest to the player. At the end of this part, your algorithm should output the name of the closest item to the console. We want to give a player a way to find an item, so make the F key trigger this operation. We need to use repeat and our array to solve this problem.")
    end

    private action InvestigateSpatializedSound10Minutes
        Section("Investigate Spatialized Sound (10 minutes)")
        Paragraph("We now have a way to find the item closest to us. For this final section, investigate the "):Link("Audio Class", "/Libraries/Sound/Audio.html"):Text(". Try to figure out as a group how you can use this information to use sound such that it tells the player if they are getting closer, or further away from, the closest item.")
    end
end
